        "text": "a side-by-side look at your filesystem and the remote FTP server\u2019s filesystem.\nBy default, FileZilla points to your home directory as the local directory (shown\nin the left-side list box).\nFIGURE 10-18:\nThe FileZilla main\nwindow.\nCHAPTER 10 Using the Internet 199\n2. Enter the hostname of the remote FTP server in the Host text box, the\nusername in the Username text box, and the password in the Password\ntext box.\nIf you\u2019ve connected to a host previously, its hostname and user login name\nappear in the text boxes.\n3. When the remote FTP session starts, a list of files and folders available\nappears in the right-side list box.\n4. Find and select the file(s) you want to download, select the folder to\ndownload them to in the left-side list box, and then drag and drop to\ntransfer the file(s).\n5. When finished, click the disconnect icon in the toolbar to disconnect and\nend the FTP session.\nIt\u2019s as simple as that. Using a graphical FTP client makes transferring lots of files",
